Scope: this commit is only the Makefile rule. git-topology.py is still
untracked and is not staged here -- adding the script itself is a
separate logical change ("topology: add git-topology") and did not seem
to belong in a build-infra commit. The unrelated README.md change is
also left unstaged.

The .py rule is deliberately appended after .sh and .sed. The earlier
question raised whether this fucks with git-delorean; it does not,
because GNU make implicit-rule search honors definition order and the
.sh rule comes first. Verified with `make -n $HOME/bin/git-delorean`
(links .sh) and `make -n $HOME/bin/git-topology` (links .py). The
fragility worth naming: that precedence is positional, not explicit, so
reordering the three link rules above .sh would silently flip delorean
to .py. Erik chose to leave it as-is rather than stash git-delorean.sh.

macOS /usr/bin/make is GNU make, so the definition-order guarantee holds
here; a strict BSD make would not behave the same, but this makefile
already relies on GNU-isms (wildcard, addprefix, pattern rules).
